   "customData": {
    "map": "card",
    "id": "d_s1b",
    "kind": "step",
    "color": "5",
    "md": "## 1a · Idea: search descriptions, open the full ticket\n**Idea:** index only the descriptions, one per ticket. The agent searches them to pick tickets, then fetches the whole ticket when it needs the details.\n- ✓ One clean vector per ticket: no comment or acceptance-criteria noise, no chunks of one ticket competing with each other.\n- ✓ The description is the ticket's own summary, written by the source, so no LLM summary to keep up to date as the corpus grows (the reason step 5 of the semantic map stopped).\n- ✗ Risk: twin families have near-identical descriptions (7 \"benchmark store + comparison UI\" tickets).\n- ✗ Risk: side details (qst_0187's AC7) aren't in the description, so the question has to match the ticket's topic."
   }
  },
