    "map": "card",
    "id": "d_s2",
    "kind": "step",
    "color": "5",
    "md": "## 2 · Slack: 35 channels, one vector per thread (16 Nov)\n**Why:** the biggest source, 285,605 documents (55.8% of the corpus); 6 of its 13 semantic questions fail.\n- Unique threads: 281.6k–283.9k, depending on what counts as a copy (0.6–1% exact duplicates; 7,641 threads share their first message with another).\n- **35 channels hold 96.8%** of threads; the other 9,042 are group chats with no channel. 27 channels have 1,000+ threads; the top 10 hold 63% (incidents 24k, eng-platform 23k, eng-runtime 22k…).\n- The title is the channel name, so about 8,000 threads share each title: it tells search nothing.\n- Each thread is one vector, so a long thread (31+ messages, the top 10%) gets squeezed into one.\nReview page with 50 threads (short / long / random + 5 most similar): `exploration/document_review/`."
   }
  },
