   "text": "Why: the biggest source, 285,605 documents\n(55.8% of the corpus); 6 of its 13 semantic\nquestions fail.\n• Unique threads: 281.6k–283.9k, depending on\n  what counts as a copy (0.6–1% exact duplicates;\n  7,641 threads share their first message with\n  another).\n• 35 channels hold 96.8% of threads; the other\n  9,042 are group chats with no channel. 27\n  channels have 1,000+ threads; the top 10 hold\n  63% (incidents 24k, eng-platform 23k, eng-runtime\n  22k…).\n• The title is the channel name, so about 8,000\n  threads share each title: it tells search nothing.\n• Each thread is one vector, so a long thread (31+\n  messages, the top 10%) gets squeezed into one.\nReview page with 50 threads (short / long / random\n+ 5 most similar): exploration/document_review/.",
   "originalText": "Why: the biggest source, 285,605 documents\n(55.8% of the corpus); 6 of its 13 semantic\nquestions fail.\n• Unique threads: 281.6k–283.9k, depending on\n  what counts as a copy (0.6–1% exact duplicates;\n  7,641 threads share their first message with\n  another).\n• 35 channels hold 96.8% of threads; the other\n  9,042 are group chats with no channel. 27\n  channels have 1,000+ threads; the top 10 hold\n  63% (incidents 24k, eng-platform 23k, eng-runtime\n  22k…).\n• The title is the channel name, so about 8,000\n  threads share each title: it tells search nothing.\n• Each thread is one vector, so a long thread (31+\n  messages, the top 10%) gets squeezed into one.\nReview page with 50 threads (short / long / random\n+ 5 most similar): exploration/document_review/.",
