    "map": "card",
    "id": "d_s2a",
    "kind": "step",
    "color": "5",
    "md": "## 2a · Idea: a channel filter for the RAG\n**Idea:** keep the parsed channel as metadata and let retrieval use it: the agent searches within chosen channels (search(query, channel=…)), or channels matching the question get a boost.\n- ✓ Free and exact: the parser already reads the channel of 96.8% of threads.\n- ✓ Shrinks the pool: the largest channel has 24k threads instead of 286k.\n- ✓ Helps when the question implies the channel: qst_0224 asks about \"public documentation\", and its answer is in #docs.\n- ✗ Hurts when the answer is in an unexpected channel: qst_0229 asks about credential signing, and its answer is in #sales. A hard filter makes that a certain miss, so it works better as an agent tool or a soft boost.\n- Same idea across sources: a source filter when the question says \"email thread\", \"call\" or \"ticket\" (brainstorm 006)."
   }
  },
