    "id": "n0",
    "kind": "problem",
    "color": "6",
    "md": "# Semantic search failures: only 52.8% correct\nWe are building a RAG system (search + LLM answer) over **EnterpriseRAG-Bench**: 512k synthetic company documents (Slack, Gmail, Jira, Drive, meeting transcripts…) and 500 test questions.\n\nMost question types score 80–100%. **Semantic questions** (125, paraphrased so they share few words with the document) score only 52.8%. Why?"
   }
  },
  {
