    "map": "card",
    "id": "d_s3",
    "kind": "step",
    "color": "5",
    "md": "## 3 · Proposal: our own schema, one SLM pass (16 Nov)\n**Why:** existing ontologies (Teamwork Graph, APQC, ITIL, GraphRAG…) don't fit our data or show nothing we can use, so we define what to mine ourselves. The near-twins differ by attributes (customer, region, date, numbers), so the schema is entities, not topics.\n**Plan:** a small model (Qwen3.5-2B + LoRA, as in the fact-extraction run) mines every document once.\n- labels for 3k–10k documents, DeepSeek V4.1 Flash: **$1–5** (measured: ≈$1 per 3k compact, ≈$4.80 per 10k)\n- label spot check, Gemini: ~$0.50–4\n- LoRA run on 1 × RTX 4090: **~$1** per run, 70 min (measured $1.01); ~$2–5 with retries\n- mining 512k with vLLM: **~$10–25**, 1–2 days on one 4090 (estimate: ~820M input, ~200M output tokens)\n- **total ~$15–35**, 2–3 days\nFor comparison: DeepSeek on all 512k ≈ $250, Gemini ≈ $1,400.\n✗ Unknown: inference speed. We measured only plain generate, 25 s per document (≈150 days, ≈$1,500 for 512k).\n→ Superseded by step 5: zero-shot extractors first, this LoRA route only as the fallback."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "text-d_s3-0",
