   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 1321797927,
   "version": 22,
   "versionNonce": 725393100,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1795607209620,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Why: existing ontologies (Teamwork Graph, APQC,\nITIL, GraphRAG…) don't fit our data or show\nnothing we can use, so we define what to mine\nourselves. The near-twins differ by attributes\n(customer, region, date, numbers), so the schema\nis entities, not topics.\nPlan: a small model (Qwen3.5-2B + LoRA, as in the\nfact-extraction run) mines every document once.\n• labels for 3k–10k documents, DeepSeek V4.1\n  Flash: $1–5 (measured: ≈$1 per 3k compact,\n  ≈$4.80 per 10k)\n• label spot check, Gemini: ~$0.50–4\n• LoRA run on 1 × RTX 4090: ~$1 per run, 70 min\n  (measured $1.01); ~$2–5 with retries\n• mining 512k with vLLM: ~$10–25, 1–2 days on\n  one 4090 (estimate: ~820M input, ~200M output\n  tokens)\n• total ~$15–35, 2–3 days\nFor comparison: DeepSeek on all 512k ≈ $250,\nGemini ≈ $1,400.\n✗ Unknown: inference speed. We measured only\nplain generate, 25 s per document (≈150 days,\n≈$1,500 for 512k).\n→ Superseded by step 5: zero-shot extractors first,\nthis LoRA route only as the fallback.",
   "originalText": "Why: existing ontologies (Teamwork Graph, APQC,\nITIL, GraphRAG…) don't fit our data or show\nnothing we can use, so we define what to mine\nourselves. The near-twins differ by attributes\n(customer, region, date, numbers), so the schema\nis entities, not topics.\nPlan: a small model (Qwen3.5-2B + LoRA, as in the\nfact-extraction run) mines every document once.\n• labels for 3k–10k documents, DeepSeek V4.1\n  Flash: $1–5 (measured: ≈$1 per 3k compact,\n  ≈$4.80 per 10k)\n• label spot check, Gemini: ~$0.50–4\n• LoRA run on 1 × RTX 4090: ~$1 per run, 70 min\n  (measured $1.01); ~$2–5 with retries\n• mining 512k with vLLM: ~$10–25, 1–2 days on\n  one 4090 (estimate: ~820M input, ~200M output\n  tokens)\n• total ~$15–35, 2–3 days\nFor comparison: DeepSeek on all 512k ≈ $250,\nGemini ≈ $1,400.\n✗ Unknown: inference speed. We measured only\nplain generate, 25 s per document (≈150 days,\n≈$1,500 for 512k).\n→ Superseded by step 5: zero-shot extractors first,\nthis LoRA route only as the fallback.",
