   "customData": {
    "map": "card",
    "id": "d_dec3",
    "kind": "decision",
    "color": "4",
    "md": "### ✓ Decision (16 Nov): mining with an LM is the path\n- **Search already reaches the right topic.** In the 41 failures the documents that beat the right one are on its topic: near-twins from one template (brainstorm 006). What's missing is depth inside the topic: which customer, region, date or number.\n- **That needs attributes the text doesn't state** (\"a healthcare client\" = CytoHealth, \"a payments company\" = Greenfield), which only a language model can mine.\n- Keywords per document are what BM25 already does (tokens, stopwords, stemming), and the fine-tuned gte vector already holds the topic.\n- So: one SLM pass with our own schema (this step), as planned. Rules and NER for the attributes the text states (names, regions, ids, dates)."
   }
  },
