   "text": "Why: check the 61–62% estimate with real search\ninstead of the candidates.\nToday's hybrid search, 300 deep, then the reranker\nover all 300. Only 20% of these documents have\nfacts; the rest use their first 2k characters. 46\nfailures:\n• In the fused 300: 20 (at 50: 7).\n• ✓ Full text @300: recall@5 20% (9), recall@10\n  22%. ~20 s per question.\n• ✗ Facts / 2k @300: recall@5 11% (5), recall@10\n  20%. ~4.7 s.\n• ✗ Full text @50 (today's depth): recall@5 4% (2),\n  ~3.8 s.\n• ✗ Text + facts (RRF): recall@5 17%.\n• In the list but not top 5: rank 6–139, median 24. A\n  deeper list holds more near-duplicates.\n• None of today's top-5 hits lost. Passing questions\n  not tested.\n→ semantic at most 52.8% → 60.0% (full text),\n56.8% (facts). Estimate was too optimistic.",
   "originalText": "Why: check the 61–62% estimate with real search\ninstead of the candidates.\nToday's hybrid search, 300 deep, then the reranker\nover all 300. Only 20% of these documents have\nfacts; the rest use their first 2k characters. 46\nfailures:\n• In the fused 300: 20 (at 50: 7).\n• ✓ Full text @300: recall@5 20% (9), recall@10\n  22%. ~20 s per question.\n• ✗ Facts / 2k @300: recall@5 11% (5), recall@10\n  20%. ~4.7 s.\n• ✗ Full text @50 (today's depth): recall@5 4% (2),\n  ~3.8 s.\n• ✗ Text + facts (RRF): recall@5 17%.\n• In the list but not top 5: rank 6–139, median 24. A\n  deeper list holds more near-duplicates.\n• None of today's top-5 hits lost. Passing questions\n  not tested.\n→ semantic at most 52.8% → 60.0% (full text),\n56.8% (facts). Estimate was too optimistic.",
   "fontSize": 20,
