   "updated": 1795607209661,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "customData": {
    "map": "card",
    "id": "d_dec5",
    "kind": "decision",
    "color": "4",
    "md": "### ✓ Decision (16 Nov): the split\n- **Concrete fields** (customer, region, dates, ids, people) → GLiNER2 or NuExtract, zero-shot, from our schema.\n- **Abstracted attributes** (industry, customer size, document purpose) → GLiNER2's classification, zero-shot.\n- **Fine-tune only if that's too weak** (step 3's LoRA, ~$15–35, as the fallback).\n- **Store scores, not just labels:** a filter can be tightened later without another pass. Calibrated probabilities aren't a reason to pick a model.\n- Mined fields become **agent tools or soft filters**, not hard routing."
   }
  },
