   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "• Concrete fields (customer, region, dates, ids,\n  people) → GLiNER2 or NuExtract, zero-shot, from\n  our schema.\n• Abstracted attributes (industry, customer size,\n  document purpose) → GLiNER2's classification,\n  zero-shot.\n• Fine-tune only if that's too weak (step 3's LoRA,\n  ~$15–35, as the fallback).\n• Store scores, not just labels: a filter can be\n  tightened later without another pass. Calibrated\n  probabilities aren't a reason to pick a model.\n• Mined fields become agent tools or soft filters, not\n  hard routing.",
   "originalText": "• Concrete fields (customer, region, dates, ids,\n  people) → GLiNER2 or NuExtract, zero-shot, from\n  our schema.\n• Abstracted attributes (industry, customer size,\n  document purpose) → GLiNER2's classification,\n  zero-shot.\n• Fine-tune only if that's too weak (step 3's LoRA,\n  ~$15–35, as the fallback).\n• Store scores, not just labels: a filter can be\n  tightened later without another pass. Calibrated\n  probabilities aren't a reason to pick a model.\n• Mined fields become agent tools or soft filters, not\n  hard routing.",
