    "map": "card",
    "id": "d_next5",
    "kind": "open",
    "color": "3",
    "md": "### ? Next (updated 16 Nov)\n1. ✓ Draft Slack schema: 19 span types (topic, person, team, client, region, product, feature, component, model, version, environment, bug, cause, fix, config, metric, identifier, date_time, document) + 11 relations. Decisions and thread kind left out (sentences, not spans). Full table in the task note.\n2. Compare **gliner2-large-v1** (340M, ~512 tokens, spans ≤ 8 words) and **gliner2.5-base-v1** (194M, 4,096 window, any span length). Both fit the laptop GPU (RTX 2000 Ada, 8 GB).\n3. Reference: DeepSeek, exact spans, ≈ $0.0009 a thread (ask first) + a hand check of 30–50.\n4. Score: precision, recall, F1 per field and per relation; micro + macro; exact + partial match; type confusion; threshold sweep per field.\n5. Rollout: 13-thread trial → adjust → ~200 threads → dev pilot (~40k docs) → full Slack pass.\nOnly if classification is needed and weak: decision models (Clef-flash; Jev or Gemini paid)."
   }
  },
