   "text": "1. ✓ Draft Slack schema: 19 span types (topic,\n    person, team, client, region, product, feature,\n    component, model, version, environment, bug,\n    cause, fix, config, metric, identifier, date_time,\n    document) + 11 relations. Decisions and thread\n    kind left out (sentences, not spans). Full table in\n    the task note.\n2. Compare gliner2-large-v1 (340M, ~512 tokens,\n    spans ≤ 8 words) and gliner2.5-base-v1 (194M,\n    4,096 window, any span length). Both fit the\n    laptop GPU (RTX 2000 Ada, 8 GB).\n3. Reference: DeepSeek, exact spans, ≈ $0.0009 a\n    thread (ask first) + a hand check of 30–50.\n4. Score: precision, recall, F1 per field and per\n    relation; micro + macro; exact + partial match;\n    type confusion; threshold sweep per field.\n5. Rollout: 13-thread trial → adjust → ~200 threads\n    → dev pilot (~40k docs) → full Slack pass.\nOnly if classification is needed and weak: decision\nmodels (Clef-flash; Jev or Gemini paid).",
   "originalText": "1. ✓ Draft Slack schema: 19 span types (topic,\n    person, team, client, region, product, feature,\n    component, model, version, environment, bug,\n    cause, fix, config, metric, identifier, date_time,\n    document) + 11 relations. Decisions and thread\n    kind left out (sentences, not spans). Full table in\n    the task note.\n2. Compare gliner2-large-v1 (340M, ~512 tokens,\n    spans ≤ 8 words) and gliner2.5-base-v1 (194M,\n    4,096 window, any span length). Both fit the\n    laptop GPU (RTX 2000 Ada, 8 GB).\n3. Reference: DeepSeek, exact spans, ≈ $0.0009 a\n    thread (ask first) + a hand check of 30–50.\n4. Score: precision, recall, F1 per field and per\n    relation; micro + macro; exact + partial match;\n    type confusion; threshold sweep per field.\n5. Rollout: 13-thread trial → adjust → ~200 threads\n    → dev pilot (~40k docs) → full Slack pass.\nOnly if classification is needed and weak: decision\nmodels (Clef-flash; Jev or Gemini paid).",
   "fontSize": 20,
