    "map": "card",
    "id": "d_s5b",
    "kind": "step",
    "color": "5",
    "md": "## 5b · Trial: zero-shot GLiNER on 13 Slack threads (16 Nov)\n**Why:** check the cheap extractor before labelling 200 threads.\n**Setup:** 19 span types + 11 relations; DeepSeek labels as the reference ($0.0079); code and report in `exploration/slack_extraction/`.\n- ✓ gliner2-large (384-word chunks) best: micro F1 0.41 exact / 0.48 partial, 0.83 s a thread on the laptop GPU.\n- ✗ gliner2.5-base: 0.33 / 0.40 on chunks, 0.28 / 0.32 on whole threads (the long window lowers recall).\n- ✓ Names: person 0.85, client 0.83, date_time 0.71, version 0.70.\n- ✗ Descriptive fields: feature 0.17, config 0.16, component 0.14, fix 0.09; topic 0.28.\n- ✗ Relations ≈ 0 for every type.\n- Part of the gap is the reference: long DeepSeek phrases, loose types."
   }
  },
