   "customData": {
    "map": "card",
    "id": "dg_g0",
    "kind": "problem",
    "color": "6",
    "md": "# Document growth: keeping search accurate as the corpus grows\nThe corpus (512k company documents today) keeps growing. Any per-document processing (summaries, facts, labels, buckets) must:\n- work for every new document, cheaply;\n- not lower the accuracy for documents already indexed.\n\n**Why it's its own problem:** the LLM-summary route for semantic search was stopped partly because accuracy on older documents can't be guaranteed as new ones arrive (see the semantic search failures map, step 5)."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "text-dg_g0-0",
