    "map": "card",
    "id": "dg_n17",
    "kind": "step",
    "color": "5",
    "md": "## 1 · Bucket the corpus\n**Idea:** facts don't separate near-duplicates well enough. Instead, split the 512k documents into buckets (topic → project → feature), like an index note that links every note with a one-line description. The agent reads the index, picks buckets, and searches only inside them. Scales as long as the buckets are good.\n\n**Example (qst_0178):** the topic (quantization) covers 108k docs; the feature name (\"precision annealing\") narrows it to 7."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "text-dg_n17-0",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 7260.0,
   "y": 607.0,
   "width": 244.24,
   "height": 32.5,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [
    "g-dg_n17"
   ],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
