   "customData": {
    "map": "card",
    "id": "dg_n18",
    "kind": "step",
    "color": "5",
    "md": "## 1a · Paper: TnT-LLM (Microsoft, 2024)\n[arXiv 2403.12173](https://arxiv.org/abs/2403.12173)\n\n**What it does:** an LLM summarizes every sampled item, builds a taxonomy from the summaries in many batches, then labels data; a small classifier trained on those labels sorts the rest.\n\n- ✓ Same pattern as our idea: a big model builds the taxonomy, a small model assigns at scale.\n- ✗ Needs an LLM summary per item and taxonomy passes over a large share of the data: far too many tokens for us."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "text-dg_n18-0",
