   "customData": {
    "map": "card",
    "id": "ab_s1c",
    "kind": "decision",
    "color": "4",
    "md": "### ✓ Conclusions (9 Nov)\n- The agents' extra searches rescue a few questions (semantic 52.8% → 60.8%), but where they don't, the agent is **more likely to answer wrongly than to say it doesn't know**.\n- The pipeline's 11 \"answered anyway\" are mostly ambiguous questions: article 004 found 10 cite a document that does answer. True hallucination ≈ 1 in 56.\n- For the agents, the split between \"a valid other document\" and \"a wrong near-duplicate\" is **not measured yet**."
   }
  },
