   "locked": false,
   "text": "• The agents' extra searches rescue a few\n  questions (semantic 52.8% → 60.8%), but where\n  they don't, the agent is more likely to answer\n  wrongly than to say it doesn't know.\n• The pipeline's 11 \"answered anyway\" are mostly\n  ambiguous questions: article 004 found 10 cite a\n  document that does answer. True hallucination ≈ 1\n  in 56.\n• For the agents, the split between \"a valid other\n  document\" and \"a wrong near-duplicate\" is not\n  measured yet.",
