    "kind": "step",
    "color": "5",
    "md": "## 4 · Topic modelling (16 Nov)\n**Why:** see what groups the corpus forms by itself, before we fix the schema, and whether the near-twin families share a cluster.\n**Fits \"no second pass\":** the fine-tuned gte vectors of all 512k documents already exist, so clustering them needs no new pass over the text.\nCandidates to look at:\n- **BERTopic:** our vectors → UMAP → HDBSCAN → c-TF-IDF keywords per topic; hierarchical topics; an LLM can name the topics (one call per topic, not per document).\n- **Top2Vec, FASTopic:** other embedding-based topic models.\n- **LDA / NMF:** cheap bag-of-words baselines.\n- Ready models: pretrained BERTopic models, zero-shot topic classifiers.\n- Link: the free cluster check planned in the document growth map (do the 46 failures sit in small clusters?)."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "text-d_s4-0",
   "type": "text",
