   "originalText": "Why: see what groups the corpus forms by itself,\nbefore we fix the schema, and whether the\nnear-twin families share a cluster.\nFits \"no second pass\": the fine-tuned gte vectors of\nall 512k documents already exist, so clustering\nthem needs no new pass over the text.\nCandidates to look at:\n• BERTopic: our vectors → UMAP → HDBSCAN →\n  c-TF-IDF keywords per topic; hierarchical topics;\n  an LLM can name the topics (one call per topic,\n  not per document).\n• Top2Vec, FASTopic: other embedding-based\n  topic models.\n• LDA / NMF: cheap bag-of-words baselines.\n• Ready models: pretrained BERTopic models,\n  zero-shot topic classifiers.\n• Link: the free cluster check planned in the\n  document growth map (do the 46 failures sit in\n  small clusters?).",
