   "updated": 1795607209692,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "customData": {
    "map": "card",
    "id": "d_end4",
    "kind": "stopped",
    "color": "2",
    "md": "### ⏸ Stopped: topic modelling and clustering (16 Nov)\n- ✗ Topic groups would route to the topic search already finds; the failures are inside a topic, among near-twins.\n- ✗ Clustering adds little over what we have: cosine similarity over the fine-tuned gte vectors already finds a document's neighbours (DiskANN index). Coarse groups only blur the details that separate the twins (MODE's own limitation: it can miss the single best chunk).\n- Topic-RAG and MODE were tested on one domain and up to 500 chunks, not 512k documents from one template.\n**Reopen if** the agent needs a browsable menu of areas (e.g. for broad \"high level\" questions), or on real company data, where documents don't arrive in neat template families."
   }
  },
