   "updated": 1795607209705,
   "link": "[[Rewrite the query from the chat history]]",
   "locked": false,
   "customData": {
    "map": "card",
    "id": "ev1_scope",
    "kind": "decision",
    "color": "4",
    "md": "### ✓ Decision (23 Nov): test single, already-composed questions\nThe final evaluation feeds the pipeline one standalone question, as if the query were already composed. It does not test composing a query from a chat, nor accuracy inside a conversation.\n- **Why:** in a real chat the last message often depends on earlier turns, so an LLM should compose the search query first. But that needs its own multi-turn test set, its own metrics (composed query vs last message, accuracy over the conversation) and its own budget.\n- ✓ Query composition is a separate task with its own evaluation: [[Rewrite the query from the chat history]].\n- ✗ Not in this evaluation: multi-turn chats, conversation accuracy."
   }
  },
