   "updated": 1795607209715,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "customData": {
    "map": "card",
    "id": "rp2",
    "kind": "step",
    "color": "5",
    "md": "## 2 · What the reranker buys, and a dev set to compare others (24 Nov)\n**Why:** a cheaper reranker has to keep most of what today's one adds. Measure that once, then build a set any alternative can be scored on offline.\n- Benchmark check: 125 semantic questions, the same 50 fused candidates with and without the reranker (free, local)\n- Dev reranking set: 380 semantic questions (dev 180 + dev_slack 200, no train), the candidates today's first search (hybrid-ft-union) hands the reranker, scored by gte-reranker-modernbert at 1,024 and 8,192 tokens\n- **The reranker reads 96.8 documents per question** (median 99, 71–100; gte and BM25 share only ~3, so the union is almost both top 50s): 36,798 pairs, each up to 1,024 tokens (61% get cut)\n- Files: `exploration/reranker_dev/` (build.py, data/summary.json; candidates and texts gitignored)"
   }
  },
