   "customData": {
    "map": "card",
    "id": "rp3",
    "kind": "step",
    "color": "5",
    "md": "## 3 · ColBERT as a cheaper reranker (24 Nov)\n**Idea:** ColBERT (late interaction) does the document work once, at ingestion, by storing a vector for every token. A question then costs one short encoding plus a cheap MaxSim over the stored vectors: 14 ms instead of the cross-encoder's 2.4 s.\n\nTested on the dev reranking set in two roles: replacing the cross-encoder, and as a pre-filter that passes only its best N candidates to the cross-encoder.\n- LateOn (LightOn, 149M, ModernBERT) beat GTE-ModernColBERT and was used for the comparison\n- No new library: sentence-transformers' MultiVectorEncoder"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "text-rp3-0",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 15420.0,
   "y": 3041.0,
   "width": 450.84,
   "height": 65.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [
    "g-rp3"
   ],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 500975168,
   "version": 22,
