   },
   "seed": 114399148,
   "version": 20,
   "versionNonce": 1084547238,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "id": "edge-e_rp3_rp3_cost",
     "type": "arrow"
    }
   ],
   "updated": 1795607209729,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "customData": {
    "map": "card",
    "id": "rp3_cost",
    "kind": "step",
    "color": "5",
    "md": "### Finding (24 Nov): ColBERT's own cost is small\n- Indexing costs about as much as embedding: one pass per document (~28 per second on the laptop GPU)\n- It stores ~780 vectors per document: ~100 GB for the corpus, ~13 GB compressed. Cheap to store; keep them in RAM or on local disk so reads stay fast\n- At 25 questions/s the reranker GPUs drop from ~25–30 L4s to ~8–9 (top 30) or ~3 (top 10)"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "text-rp3_cost-0",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 16020.0,
   "y": 4762.0,
   "width": 414.67,
   "height": 57.5,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
